  "user_request_original": "Design a 22-layer multilayer optical filter on CaF2 (Daimon-20) substrate with air incidence at normal angle. Stack sequence from air side: ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat), ZnS, Al2O3 (Kischkat) (22 layers total, alternating starting with ZnS, ending with Al2O3 (Kischkat) on CaF2 (Daimon-20) substrate). Optimize individual layer thicknesses for each of the 22 layers independently. Thickness bounds: 50 nm minimum, 1500 nm maximum per layer. Target behavior: high transmittance at 3.25-3.35 μm and 4.20-4.30 μm; low transmittance at 2.50-3.10 μm and 4.45-5.00 μm. No metal layers. Materials: zns and Al2O3 (Kischkat) from catalog. Substrate: CaF2 (Daimon-20). Incidence: air to stack. Evaluate transmittance and reflectance across 2500-5000 nm wavelength range.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design and optimize a 22-layer alternating ZnS/Al2O3 dielectric filter on a CaF2 substrate under normal incidence in air. Optimize all individual layer thicknesses within 50-1500 nm bounds to maximize transmission in the 3250-3350 nm and 4200-4300 nm bands while minimizing transmission in the 2500-3100 nm and 4450-5000 nm bands. Evaluate performance across 2500-5000 nm.",
